  "name": "Send tiered overdue invoice reminders with Xero, Gmail, Slack and Sheets",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "2a82149f-3fb4-4ce9-8008-1c7abdecbda4",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        816,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 848,
        "content": "## Xero Overdue Invoice Reminders\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs on a daily schedule to find unpaid Xero invoices, calculate how many days overdue they are, and assign them to reminder tiers. It checks Google Sheets to avoid sending duplicate reminders, routes eligible invoices by tier, then sends the appropriate Gmail or Slack notification. Completed reminder paths are merged and written back to Google Sheets as sent records.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect and authorize the Xero credential used to retrieve unpaid invoices.\n- Connect Gmail for sending the day 7 and day 14 reminder emails.\n- Connect Slack and confirm the account owner channel or escalation destination is available.\n- Connect Google Sheets and configure the sheet used to check and mark already-sent reminders.\n- Review the Config node values for tier1Days, tier2Days, tier3Days, and accountOwnerSlackChannel before activating the daily schedule.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the overdue-day thresholds, email copy, Slack escalation behavior, and Google Sheets tracking columns to match your collections process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
